# Tomady Nutrition — AI Coding Rules

## Commit Convention

All commits MUST follow **Conventional Commits** (v1.0.0):

```
<type>(<scope>): <short description>

[optional body]

[optional footer(s)]
```

### Types

| Type       | Usage                                      |
|------------|--------------------------------------------|
| `feat`     | A new feature                              |
| `fix`      | A bug fix                                  |
| `docs`     | Documentation only changes                 |
| `style`    | Code style (formatting, missing semicolons)|
| `refactor` | Code change that neither fixes nor adds    |
| `perf`     | Performance improvement                    |
| `test`     | Adding or correcting tests                 |
| `chore`    | Build, CI, dependencies, tooling           |
| `config`   | Configuration changes                      |

### Scopes

| Scope       | Area                          |
|-------------|-------------------------------|
| `db`        | Room entities, DAOs, database |
| `diet`      | Diet service & data layer     |
| `foodb`     | FooDB data service & layer    |
| `gemma`     | Gemma AI/ML service           |
| `worker`    | Background workers            |
| `bridge`    | React Native bridge modules   |
| `docs`      | Documentation                 |
| `build`     | Gradle, CI, project config    |

### Examples

```
feat(diet): add daily nutrition goal computation
fix(foodb): correct nutrient unit parsing from raw content
chore(build): upgrade Room to 2.6.1
docs: update architecture overview in SOUSPAPE.md
```

## Branch Naming

- `feat/<scope>/<short-desc>`
- `fix/<scope>/<short-desc>`
- `chore/<scope>/<short-desc>`

Example: `feat/diet/meal-plan-generator`

## Project Language & Style

- All new source code MUST be written in **Kotlin**.
- Use **camelCase** for variables/functions, **PascalCase** for classes/interfaces.
- Every public class MUST have a KDoc comment describing its purpose.
- Do NOT implement business logic in stubs — keep method bodies empty or returning default values.

## Documentation

- See `doc/SOUSPAPE.md` for project-specific architecture decisions and instructions.
